WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.195
So here's the brain of
 a non-procrastinator.

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:03.546
Here's my brain.

00:00:03.546 --> 00:00:06.000
Both brains have a Rational 
Decision-Maker in them,

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.501
but the procrastinator's&nbsp;brain also
 has an Instant Gratification Monkey.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:13.507
So the Rational Decision-Maker 
will make the&nbsp;rational decision

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:17.435
to do something productive, but 
the Monkey doesn't like that plan,

00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:19.394
so&nbsp;he actually takes the 
wheel, and he says,

00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:22.701
"We're not going to really have room on
 the&nbsp;schedule for any work today. Sorry!"

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:25.491
The Instant Gratification Monkey
does not seem like&nbsp;a guy

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:26.258
 you want behind the wheel.

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:29.693
He only cares about two 
things: easy and fun.

00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:33.186
Sometimes it makes&nbsp;sense to be 
doing things that are easy and fun,

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:37.167
but other times, it makes much 
more sense to be&nbsp;doing things

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:40.897
that are harder and less pleasant, 
for the sake of the big picture.

00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:42.862
And&nbsp;that's when we 
have a conflict.

00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:45.592
We need to stay aware of the 
Instant Gratification&nbsp;Monkey.

00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:48.639
We need to think about what we're
really procrastinating on,

00:00:48.639 --> 00:00:52.174
because everyone is&nbsp;procrastinating 
on something in life.

00:00:52.545 --> 00:00:55.504
That's  a job that should&nbsp;
probably start today.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.458
Well, maybe not today ...

